{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-index-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0050","math_ordinal":73,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The second sum is indexed by j and ranges over the b-sequence; the authority's b_i leaves j unused and conflicts with the concatenation in the following sentence.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt224.tex:112","source_normalized_sha256":"f8ab92d595fbedb9565ed4f18a9172abf9370689810e3420fd0241acbaa21c0a","source_text":"$\\sum_{j=1}^n|f(b_i)-f(b_{i-1})|$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt224.tex:109","target_normalized_sha256":"0c8d097058de20634ced0ed2ada3bacc878dbd43cdad3321f1272354a311f50f","target_text":"$\\sum_{j=1}^n|f(b_j)-f(b_{j-1})|$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S224"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-interval","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0051","math_ordinal":73,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"This proposition has arbitrary D and no interval [a,b]; the concatenated sequence lies in D, so the defining bound is Var_D(f), exactly as the conclusion below requires.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt224.tex:114","source_normalized_sha256":"f8ab92d595fbedb9565ed4f18a9172abf9370689810e3420fd0241acbaa21c0a","source_text":"$\\Var_{[a,b]}(f)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt224.tex:111","target_normalized_sha256":"0c8d097058de20634ced0ed2ada3bacc878dbd43cdad3321f1272354a311f50f","target_text":"$\\Var_D(f)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S224"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-function-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0053","math_ordinal":240,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof has defined h_1 and h_2 as the two monotone extensions; f_2 must be derived from h_2 for f_1-f_2 to recover f, while repeating h_1 destroys the displayed decomposition.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt224.tex:382","source_normalized_sha256":"fe4b0b4d29acfae5db5ba53f77dcef4f29c774ba9a178338c1bf1be322e21de9","source_text":"$f_2=h_1-\\gamma_2+\\beta_2$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt224.tex:381","target_normalized_sha256":"8043bee4158a0411963a112a6a3c9271b607690481f89d716bfa85a0324a964b","target_text":"$f_2=h_2-\\gamma_2+\\beta_2$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S224"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0054","math_ordinal":271,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The construction defines A_n only for n at least 1, while this corpus uses N containing 0; taking the union over n at least 1 removes the undefined A_0 without changing the discontinuity characterization.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt224.tex:430","source_normalized_sha256":"e92c314342a61aefdd7b16e2d022093e79a75a2b9e971da1d23f73395a9f0941","source_text":"$A=\\bigcup_{n\\in\\Bbb N}A_n$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt224.tex:431","target_normalized_sha256":"88909142be84f583b1b1d6dbd003830893c3d87ffcc4dead7c401447591319f1","target_text":"$A=\\bigcup_{n\\ge 1}A_n$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S224"}
{"classification":"mathematical-endpoint-proof-gap","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0055","math_ordinal":347,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The hypotheses control f only on the open interval (a,b); allowing the last sample to equal b invalidates the asserted M bound and limit. Every open mesh cell contains domain points because f is defined almost everywhere, so choosing interior samples closes the gap.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt224.tex:510","source_normalized_sha256":"a41f8b84deb78499de6db5c322717c293b3b94adb30e1aa7ad7e641ee912d74b","source_text":"$x_{nk}\\in\\dom f\\cap\\ocint{a_{n,k-1},a_{nk}}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt224.tex:515","target_normalized_sha256":"618b9460e662c2f0c560326d5f7f59db3aad863ce2c768d217117a9e5859b232","target_text":"$x_{nk}\\in\\dom f\\cap\\ooint{a_{n,k-1},a_{nk}}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S224"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-domain-qualifier","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0056","math_ordinal":393,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The section permits partial functions and the real-valued decomposition in 224D is explicitly asserted only on D intersect dom f; the complex analogue requires the same domain qualifier.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt224.tex:600","source_normalized_sha256":"3f39d5c348e5b79d06e842c114e6cc571583bbf44e4b0ebfda1a01ec05745d43","source_text":"$f=f_1-f_2+if_3-if_4$ on $D$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt224.tex:603","target_normalized_sha256":"50abf24fe5788eaf714a10fed80bd66d1b53137b9a6bd61213ed14a0fd4e3919","target_text":"$f=f_1-f_2+if_3-if_4$ pada $D\\cap\\dom f$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S224"}
